IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `claq-dates`

-- Civil Liability Act 2003 (Queensland) -- chapter 2, part 2A (liability of institutions for child abuse), as the
-- CLAIMANT meets it.
--
-- SEAT: the person who was abused as a child and claims against the institution. "Is my claim an abuse claim?",
-- "Must I prove the institution failed to prevent it?", "Whom can I sue, if the institution was or is unincorporated?",
-- "When can I ask the court to make the trustee of its trust the defendant?", "Did the institution identify its trusts
-- in time?", "What can my judgment or settlement be paid from?".
--
-- One regulative rule: s 33H(7)(a), the institution's duty, under a court order, to identify its associated trusts and
-- give information about them within 28 days or the period the court sets. It is run by EVALTRACE inside an exported
-- question that takes only dates and yes/no facts.
--
-- Unofficial version. Based on content from the Queensland Legislation website at 6 November 2026. (c) The State of
-- Queensland, CC BY 4.0. See SOURCE-LICENSE.md.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Civil Liability Act 2003: claims against institutions for child abuse`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `ss 33A, 33C -- an abuse claim`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- s 33A "abuse, of a child-- (a) for division 2--means sexual abuse or serious physical abuse of the child; or (b)
-- otherwise, means-- (i) sexual abuse or serious physical abuse of the child; or (ii) psychological abuse of the child
-- perpetrated in connection with sexual abuse or serious physical abuse of the child." Two "means" definitions.
DECLARE `What was done to me as a child` IS ONE OF
    `sexual abuse`
    `serious physical abuse`
    `psychological abuse in connection with sexual abuse or serious physical abuse`
    `psychological abuse alone, or other harm`

GIVEN `what was done` IS A `What was done to me as a child`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 33A -- abuse, for division 2` `what was done` IF
    (`what was done` EQUALS `sexual abuse`) OR (`what was done` EQUALS `serious physical abuse`)

GIVEN `what was done` IS A `What was done to me as a child`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 33A -- abuse, otherwise` `what was done` IF
    `s 33A -- abuse, for division 2` `what was done`
    OR (`what was done` EQUALS `psychological abuse in connection with sexual abuse or serious physical abuse`)

-- s 33C(1) "the persons associated with an institution include-- (a) an officer, office holder, representative,
-- leader, owner, member, employee, agent, volunteer or contractor of the institution; and (b) for ... a religious
-- organisation--a minister of religion, religious leader or member of the personnel ...; and (c) [a delegate of care,
-- supervision, control or authority over the child, if an individual, and the persons who would be in (a) or (b) if the
-- delegate were the institution]; and (d) a person prescribed by regulation" (none is prescribed in the deposited
-- Civil Liability Regulation 2025). An "includes" list: a person not on it is "not covered" (the court decides).
-- (2) not "only because a child protection order is made granting long-term guardianship"; (3) not "only because the
-- person is associated with an entity that is funded or regulated by the institution". Flat negatives.
DECLARE `Who the abuser was to the institution` IS ONE OF
    `an officer, office holder, representative, leader, owner, member, employee, agent, volunteer or contractor of it`
    `a minister of religion, religious leader or member of the personnel of it, a religious organisation`
    `an individual to whom it delegated care, supervision, control or authority over me, or such a person of a delegate entity`
    `connected to it only through an entity it funds or regulates`
    `my long-term guardian under a child protection order, and nothing more`
    `someone else`

-- s 33A "institution-- (a) means an entity that provides an activity, program or service of a kind that gives an
-- opportunity for a person to have contact with a child; and (b) includes a public sector unit that is [such] an
-- entity ...; and (c) does not include a family." s 33A "abuse claim means a claim arising from the abuse of a child by
-- a person associated with an institution while the child was under the care, supervision, control or authority of the
-- institution."
DECLARE `Is my claim an abuse claim` IS ONE OF
    `yes: my claim is an abuse claim under part 2A (s 33A)`
    `no: what was done is not abuse as part 2A defines it (s 33A)`
    `no: a family is not an institution, nor is an entity whose activities give no opportunity for contact with a child (s 33A)`
    `no: I was not under the institution's care, supervision, control or authority at the time (s 33A)`
    `no: a person is not associated with the institution only because of a long-term guardianship order (s 33C(2))`
    `no: a person is not associated with the institution only because they are associated with an entity it funds or regulates (s 33C(3))`
    `not covered: s 33C lists those associated with an institution without closing the list; whether this person is associated is for the court`

GIVEN `what was done` IS A `What was done to me as a child`
      `an entity giving contact with children, not a family` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the abuser` IS A `Who the abuser was to the institution`
      `under its care, supervision, control or authority` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Is my claim an abuse claim`
`s 33A -- an abuse claim` `what was done` `an entity giving contact with children, not a family` `the abuser` `under its care, supervision, control or authority` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`s 33A -- abuse, otherwise` `what was done`) THEN `no: what was done is not abuse as part 2A defines it (s 33A)`
        IF NOT (`an entity giving contact with children, not a family`) THEN `no: a family is not an institution, nor is an entity whose activities give no opportunity for contact with a child (s 33A)`
        IF NOT (`under its care, supervision, control or authority`) THEN `no: I was not under the institution's care, supervision, control or authority at the time (s 33A)`
        IF `the abuser` EQUALS `my long-term guardian under a child protection order, and nothing more` THEN `no: a person is not associated with the institution only because of a long-term guardianship order (s 33C(2))`
        IF `the abuser` EQUALS `connected to it only through an entity it funds or regulates` THEN `no: a person is not associated with the institution only because they are associated with an entity it funds or regulates (s 33C(3))`
        IF `the abuser` EQUALS `someone else` THEN `not covered: s 33C lists those associated with an institution without closing the list; whether this person is associated is for the court`
        OTHERWISE `yes: my claim is an abuse claim under part 2A (s 33A)`

@export Is my claim about abuse I suffered as a child an "abuse claim" against an institution under the Civil Liability Act 2003 (Qld) part 2A (ss 33A, 33C)? It is if you suffered sexual abuse, serious physical abuse, or psychological abuse connected with either, by a person associated with the institution, while you were in its care, supervision, control or authority. An institution is any entity (including a government body) whose activities, programs or services give an opportunity for contact with children, but not a family. Associated persons include its officers, employees, members, volunteers, contractors and agents, and the clergy and personnel of a religious organisation.
GIVEN `what was done` IS A `What was done to me as a child` @desc What was done to you as a child: sexual abuse; serious physical abuse; psychological abuse in connection with sexual or serious physical abuse; or psychological abuse alone, or other harm
      `institution gives contact with children` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the organisation provides an activity, program or service of a kind that gives an opportunity for contact with a child (a school, church, club, care provider or government body, for example), and is not your family
      `abuser's link` IS A `Who the abuser was to the institution` @desc Who the abuser was to the institution
      `in its care` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were under the care, supervision, control or authority of the institution when the abuse happened
GIVETH A `Is my claim an abuse claim`
`Is my claim an abuse claim` MEANS
    `s 33A -- an abuse claim` `what was done` `institution gives contact with children` `abuser's link` `in its care`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `ss 33D, 33E, 86 -- the institution's duty, and who must prove what`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- s 33D "An institution has a duty to take all reasonable steps to prevent the abuse of a child by a person associated
-- with the institution while the child is under the care, supervision, control or authority of the institution."
-- s 33E(2) "The institution is taken to have breached its duty under section 33D unless the institution proves it took
-- all reasonable steps to prevent the abuse." s 86: part 2A, "other than division 2", applies to causes of action
-- arising before or after its commencement: division 2 only to abuse after it commenced (the day is not in the
-- deposited text: asked; fork F9).
DECLARE `Must I prove the institution was at fault` IS ONE OF
    `no: the institution is taken to have breached its duty to prevent the abuse unless it proves it took all reasonable steps (s 33E(2))`
    `no breach under s 33D: the institution proved it took all reasonable steps to prevent the abuse (s 33E(2))`
    `s 33E does not apply: division 2 covers only sexual abuse or serious physical abuse (s 33A(a))`
    `s 33E does not apply: the abuse happened before division 2 of part 2A commenced (s 86); the general law of negligence decides`
    `s 33E does not apply: my claim is not an abuse claim by a person associated with the institution while I was in its care`

GIVEN `what was done` IS A `What was done to me as a child`
      `an abuse claim` IS A BOOLEAN
      `after division 2 commenced` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the institution proves all reasonable steps` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Must I prove the institution was at fault`
`ss 33D, 33E -- presumed breach of the duty to prevent abuse` `what was done` `an abuse claim` `after division 2 commenced` `the institution proves all reasonable steps` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`an abuse claim`) THEN `s 33E does not apply: my claim is not an abuse claim by a person associated with the institution while I was in its care`
        IF NOT (`s 33A -- abuse, for division 2` `what was done`) THEN `s 33E does not apply: division 2 covers only sexual abuse or serious physical abuse (s 33A(a))`
        IF NOT (`after division 2 commenced`) THEN `s 33E does not apply: the abuse happened before division 2 of part 2A commenced (s 86); the general law of negligence decides`
        IF `the institution proves all reasonable steps` THEN `no breach under s 33D: the institution proved it took all reasonable steps to prevent the abuse (s 33E(2))`
        OTHERWISE `no: the institution is taken to have breached its duty to prevent the abuse unless it proves it took all reasonable steps (s 33E(2))`

@export Do I have to prove that the institution failed to prevent the abuse I suffered as a child (Civil Liability Act 2003 (Qld) ss 33D, 33E)? An institution has a duty to take all reasonable steps to prevent sexual or serious physical abuse of a child in its care by a person associated with it. If such abuse happened, the institution is taken to have breached that duty unless it proves it took all reasonable steps, judged by its nature, its resources, its relationship with the child and the position it gave the abuser. This applies only to abuse after division 2 of part 2A commenced.
GIVEN `what was done` IS A `What was done to me as a child` @desc What was done to you as a child: sexual abuse; serious physical abuse; psychological abuse in connection with either; or psychological abuse alone, or other harm
      `abuse claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the abuse was by a person associated with the institution while you were under its care, supervision, control or authority (see the question whether your claim is an abuse claim)
      `after division 2 commenced` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the abuse happened after the Civil Liability Act 2003 chapter 2, part 2A, division 2 (the institution's duty) commenced
      `institution proves reasonable steps` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the institution proves it took all reasonable steps to prevent the abuse
GIVETH A `Must I prove the institution was at fault`
`Must I prove the institution was at fault` MEANS
    `ss 33D, 33E -- presumed breach of the duty to prevent abuse` `what was done` `abuse claim` `after division 2 commenced` `institution proves reasonable steps`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `ss 33F-33I, 33O, 33P -- whom I can sue`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- s 33F: if, when my cause of action accrued, the institution was unincorporated and I had a cause of action against a
-- former office holder founded on their responsibility for the institution or the abuser, and the institution is now
-- incorporated, "a proceeding for the claimant's cause of action may be started or continued against the institution".
-- s 33G: if it is still unincorporated and the former office holder no longer holds the office, the proceeding "may be
-- started or continued against the current holder of the relevant office ... in the name of the office" (s 33P: the
-- current head, where no such office remains). s 33H(2): "A proceeding for an abuse claim may be started against the
-- [unincorporated] institution." (3) notice of a claim under the Personal Injuries Proceedings Act 2002 s 9(1) "must be
-- given to the head of the institution". s 33I(a): if there is a nominee, "a proceeding for an abuse claim may be started
-- or continued against the nominee". s 33O: an institution that is substantially the same, or a relevant successor, is
-- the same institution (asked).
DECLARE `Whom I can sue` HAS
    `the institution itself` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the institution, for the liability of a former office holder (s 33F)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the current holder of the office, in the name of the office (s 33G)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the institution's nominee (s 33I)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `my notice of claim goes to the head of the institution (s 33H(3))` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `incorporated now` IS A BOOLEAN
      `unincorporated when my cause accrued` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a cause against a former office holder` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the former office holder still holds the office` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is a nominee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Whom I can sue`
`ss 33F-33I -- whom I can sue` `incorporated now` `unincorporated when my cause accrued` `a cause against a former office holder` `the former office holder still holds the office` `there is a nominee` MEANS
    `Whom I can sue` WITH
        `the institution itself` IS TRUE
        `the institution, for the liability of a former office holder (s 33F)` IS `incorporated now` AND `unincorporated when my cause accrued` AND `a cause against a former office holder`
        `the current holder of the office, in the name of the office (s 33G)` IS (NOT (`incorporated now`)) AND `unincorporated when my cause accrued` AND `a cause against a former office holder` AND (NOT (`the former office holder still holds the office`))
        `the institution's nominee (s 33I)` IS (NOT (`incorporated now`)) AND `there is a nominee`
        `my notice of claim goes to the head of the institution (s 33H(3))` IS NOT (`incorporated now`)

@export Whom can I sue for the abuse I suffered as a child, if the institution was, or still is, an unincorporated body such as a church, club or association (Civil Liability Act 2003 (Qld) ss 33F-33I, 33O, 33P)? An incorporated institution can be sued, and if it was unincorporated when your cause of action arose it answers for the liability of the office holder you could have sued then. An unincorporated institution can itself be sued (your notice of claim goes to its head), or its nominee if it has one; and the current holder of the office (or, if the office is gone, the head) can be sued in the name of the office where the former office holder has left it. An institution that has changed its name, structure or place, become incorporated, or merged into a successor is treated as the same institution.
GIVEN `incorporated now` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the institution (or its successor) is now an incorporated body
      `unincorporated then` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the institution was an unincorporated body when your cause of action arose
      `claim against former office holder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have or had a cause of action against a person who then held an office of authority in the institution (for example a management committee member, bishop or head), founded on their responsibility for the institution or the abuser
      `office holder still in office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that person still holds that office
      `institution has nominee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the institution has nominated a person (with their consent) as the appropriate defendant, or the court has ordered a trustee to be its nominee
GIVETH A `Whom I can sue`
`Whom can I sue for the abuse` MEANS
    `ss 33F-33I -- whom I can sue` `incorporated now` `unincorporated then` `claim against former office holder` `office holder still in office` `institution has nominee`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `s 33H(5), (6) -- asking the court to make a trust's trustee the nominee`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- s 33H(5) "Subsection (6) applies if-- (a) at least 120 days have passed since a proceeding for an abuse claim was
-- started against the institution; and (b) either-- (i) there is no nominee for the institution; or (ii) a court is
-- satisfied the institution's nominee does not have sufficient assets ...". (6) "On application by the claimant, a
-- court may order that the trustee of a trust is the institution's nominee if the court is satisfied" the trust is or
-- was an associated trust (and, if it no longer is, it was cut off to avoid paying abuse claims), and the order would
-- be appropriate. "At least 120 days have passed since" the day started: from the day 120 days after it (fork F8).
GIVEN `the day started` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 33H(5)(a) -- the first day I may apply` `the day started` MEANS `the day` 120 `days after` `the day started`

DECLARE `May I apply for a trustee to be made the nominee` IS ONE OF
    `yes: I may apply, and the court may order it if satisfied the trust is or was an associated trust and the order is appropriate (s 33H(6))`
    `not yet: 120 days have not passed since my proceeding was started (s 33H(5)(a))`
    `no: the institution has a nominee and the court is not satisfied it lacks sufficient assets (s 33H(5)(b))`
    `no: s 33H applies only to an unincorporated institution (s 33H(1))`

GIVEN `unincorporated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day started` IS A DATE
      `the day I apply` IS A DATE
      `there is a nominee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the nominee lacks sufficient assets` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `May I apply for a trustee to be made the nominee`
`s 33H(5), (6) -- applying for a trustee nominee` `unincorporated` `the day started` `the day I apply` `there is a nominee` `the nominee lacks sufficient assets` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`unincorporated`) THEN `no: s 33H applies only to an unincorporated institution (s 33H(1))`
        IF `there is a nominee` AND (NOT (`the nominee lacks sufficient assets`)) THEN `no: the institution has a nominee and the court is not satisfied it lacks sufficient assets (s 33H(5)(b))`
        IF `the date` `the day I apply` `falls before` (`s 33H(5)(a) -- the first day I may apply` `the day started`) THEN `not yet: 120 days have not passed since my proceeding was started (s 33H(5)(a))`
        OTHERWISE `yes: I may apply, and the court may order it if satisfied the trust is or was an associated trust and the order is appropriate (s 33H(6))`

@export May I ask the court to order that the trustee of a trust the institution uses (for example a church property trust) be made the defendant for my abuse claim (Civil Liability Act 2003 (Qld) s 33H(5), (6))? For an unincorporated institution, once at least 120 days have passed since your proceeding was started, if there is no nominee, or the court is satisfied the nominee does not have enough assets, you may apply; the court may make the order if the trust is or was an associated trust of the institution (and, if no longer, was separated to avoid paying abuse claims) and the order is appropriate.
GIVEN `unincorporated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the institution is an unincorporated body
      `day proceeding started` IS A DATE @desc The day your proceeding for the abuse claim was started against the institution, as an ISO date
      `day of application` IS A DATE @desc The day you would apply, as an ISO date
      `has nominee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the institution has a nominee
      `nominee lacks assets` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it has: whether the court is satisfied the nominee does not have sufficient assets to satisfy a liability that may be found on your claim
GIVETH A `May I apply for a trustee to be made the nominee`
`May I apply for a trustee to be made the nominee` MEANS
    `s 33H(5), (6) -- applying for a trustee nominee` `unincorporated` `day proceeding started` `day of application` `has nominee` `nominee lacks assets`

@export From what day may I apply for a trust's trustee to be made the institution's nominee (Civil Liability Act 2003 (Qld) s 33H(5)(a))? The day 120 days after your proceeding against the unincorporated institution was started; the other conditions are in the question whether you may apply.
GIVEN `day proceeding started` IS A DATE @desc The day your proceeding for the abuse claim was started against the institution, as an ISO date
GIVETH A DATE
`From what day may I apply for a trustee nominee` MEANS
    `s 33H(5)(a) -- the first day I may apply` `day proceeding started`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `s 33H(7) -- the institution's duty to identify its trusts (a regulative rule)`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- s 33H(7) "A court may-- (a) order the institution to do the following within 28 days or any other period the court
-- considers appropriate-- (i) identify to the court any trusts that are, or used to be, associated trusts of the
-- institution; (ii) provide particular information about the financial capacity of the trusts". The order is the
-- court's; once made, the institution MUST comply within the period, counted from the order (fork F10: the last day is
-- the day that many days after the order).
DECLARE `Party` IS ONE OF `the institution`
DECLARE `Act done` IS ONE OF `identify its associated trusts and give the information ordered`

GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Act done`
`s 33H(7)(a) -- identify the trusts within the period` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `the institution`
    MUST `identify its associated trusts and give the information ordered`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the institution` BECAUSE "the institution did not identify its associated trusts, and give the information about their financial capacity, within the period the court's order under s 33H(7)(a) allowed"

-- The helper that runs the rule over what happened. On the stable l4 a CONSIDER on an EVALTRACE can match FULFILLED but
-- not BREACH. It takes a DEONTIC value, so it is never exported.
GIVEN `the rule` IS A DEONTIC `Party` `Act done`
      `the time` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `done in time under` `the rule` `if done at` `the time` IF
    CONSIDER EVALTRACE `the rule` 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL `the time`), (EVENT `the institution` `identify its associated trusts and give the information ordered` `the time`))
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

DECLARE `Has the institution identified its trusts in time` IS ONE OF
    `yes: the institution complied within the period the order allowed (s 33H(7)(a))`
    `no: the institution complied, but after the period the order allowed ended (s 33H(7)(a)); the court may make further orders`
    `not yet due: the institution has not complied, but the period has not ended`
    `no: the period the order allowed has ended and the institution has not complied (s 33H(7)(a)); the court may make further orders`

GIVEN `the day of the order` IS A DATE
      `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
      `it has complied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day it complied` IS A DATE
      `today` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Has the institution identified its trusts in time`
`s 33H(7)(a) -- compliance with the order` `the day of the order` `the days allowed` `it has complied` `the day it complied` `today` MEANS
    IF `it has complied`
    THEN IF `done in time under` (`s 33H(7)(a) -- identify the trusts within the period` `the days allowed`) `if done at` (`the number of days from` `the day of the order` `until` `the day it complied`)
         THEN `yes: the institution complied within the period the order allowed (s 33H(7)(a))`
         ELSE `no: the institution complied, but after the period the order allowed ended (s 33H(7)(a)); the court may make further orders`
    ELSE IF `done in time under` (`s 33H(7)(a) -- identify the trusts within the period` `the days allowed`) `if done at` (`the number of days from` `the day of the order` `until` `today`)
         THEN `not yet due: the institution has not complied, but the period has not ended`
         ELSE `no: the period the order allowed has ended and the institution has not complied (s 33H(7)(a)); the court may make further orders`

@export The court ordered the institution to identify its associated trusts and give information about their finances. Has it done so in time (Civil Liability Act 2003 (Qld) s 33H(7))? The order requires it within 28 days, or another period the court sets, counted from the order.
GIVEN `day of order` IS A DATE @desc The day the court made the order, as an ISO date
      `days allowed` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of days the order allows: 28 unless the court set another period
      `has complied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the institution has identified the trusts and given the information ordered
      `day complied` IS A DATE @desc If it has: the day it did so, as an ISO date (otherwise any date)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date, as an ISO date
GIVETH A `Has the institution identified its trusts in time`
`Has the institution identified its trusts in time` MEANS
    `s 33H(7)(a) -- compliance with the order` `day of order` `days allowed` `has complied` `day complied` `today`

GIVEN `the day of the order` IS A DATE, `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`s 33H(7)(a) -- the last day to comply` `the day of the order` `the days allowed` MEANS `the day` `the days allowed` `days after` `the day of the order`

@export By what day must the institution identify its associated trusts under the court's order (Civil Liability Act 2003 (Qld) s 33H(7)(a))? The day 28 days (or the period the court set) after the order.
GIVEN `day of order` IS A DATE @desc The day the court made the order, as an ISO date
      `days allowed` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of days the order allows: 28 unless the court set another period
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must the institution identify its trusts` MEANS
    `s 33H(7)(a) -- the last day to comply` `day of order` `days allowed`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `ss 33B, 33J-33MA -- what a judgment or settlement can be paid from`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- s 33B(1) "a trust is an associated trust of an institution if the institution uses the trust to carry out its
-- functions or activities and-- (a) the institution has, directly or indirectly, [a power to control the application
-- of income or distribution of property, to obtain the beneficial enjoyment of its property or income, to appoint or
-- remove a trustee or beneficiary, or to determine the outcome of any other decision about its operations]; or (b) a
-- member or manager of the institution has, under the trust deed, a power mentioned in paragraph (a); or (c) a trustee
-- is accustomed to acting, or is under a formal or informal obligation to act, according to the directions,
-- instructions or wishes of the institution or a member or manager". (2) also a trust whose trustee is made nominee
-- under s 33H(6). A "means"-like "is ... if": worked out.
GIVEN `the institution uses it for its functions or activities` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the institution has a power over it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a member or manager has such a power under the deed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the trustee acts as the institution wishes` IS A BOOLEAN
      `its trustee was ordered to be the nominee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 33B -- an associated trust` `the institution uses it for its functions or activities` `the institution has a power over it` `a member or manager has such a power under the deed` `the trustee acts as the institution wishes` `its trustee was ordered to be the nominee` IF
        (    `the institution uses it for its functions or activities`
         AND (`the institution has a power over it` OR `a member or manager has such a power under the deed` OR `the trustee acts as the institution wishes`))
    OR  `its trustee was ordered to be the nominee`

@export Is this trust an "associated trust" of the institution, whose assets can be used to pay my abuse claim (Civil Liability Act 2003 (Qld) s 33B)? It is if the institution uses the trust to carry out its functions or activities and either the institution (or, under the trust deed, a member or manager of it) has power to control the trust's income or property, benefit from it, appoint or remove trustees or beneficiaries, or decide its operations, or the trustee is accustomed or obliged to act as the institution wishes. A trust whose trustee the court has made the institution's nominee also counts.
GIVEN `used for its functions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the institution uses the trust to carry out its functions or activities
      `institution has power` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the institution has, directly or indirectly, a power to control the application of the trust's income or distribution of its property, to obtain the benefit of its property or income, to appoint or remove a trustee or beneficiary, or to determine the outcome of any other decision about its operations
      `member has power under deed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a member or manager of the institution has such a power under the trust deed
      `trustee follows institution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a trustee is accustomed to acting, or under a formal or informal obligation to act, according to the directions, instructions or wishes of the institution or a member or manager of it
      `trustee ordered nominee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court has ordered under s 33H(6) that the trustee of this trust is the institution's nominee
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Is this trust an associated trust` MEANS
    `s 33B -- an associated trust` `used for its functions` `institution has power` `member has power under deed` `trustee follows institution` `trustee ordered nominee`

-- ss 33J-33M: the institution may satisfy the liability out of its assets and those of an associated trust (33J); a
-- nominee that is the trustee of an associated trust out of that trust's and the institution's assets (33K(2)), its
-- liability as nominee being limited to the value of the trust property (33M(4)); another nominee out of its own and the
-- institution's assets (33K(3)); a current office holder "is not personally liable" and may use the institution's and
-- an associated trust's assets (33L). s 33MA: the liability includes the costs of the proceeding.
DECLARE `The defendant I hold a judgment or settlement against` IS ONE OF
    `the institution`
    `the institution's nominee, which is the trustee of an associated trust`
    `the institution's nominee, which is not such a trustee`
    `the current holder of the office`

DECLARE `What my judgment or settlement can be paid from` IS ONE OF
    `the assets of the institution and of its associated trusts, including my costs (ss 33J, 33MA)`
    `the assets of the associated trust and of the institution, the trustee's own liability being limited to the value of the trust property, including my costs (ss 33K(2), 33M(4), 33MA)`
    `the nominee's own assets and the assets of the institution, including my costs (ss 33K(3), 33MA)`
    `the assets of the institution and of its associated trusts, not the office holder's own assets, including my costs (ss 33L, 33MA)`

GIVEN `the defendant` IS A `The defendant I hold a judgment or settlement against`
GIVETH A `What my judgment or settlement can be paid from`
`ss 33J-33MA -- what the liability is paid from` `the defendant` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the defendant`
    WHEN `the institution` THEN `the assets of the institution and of its associated trusts, including my costs (ss 33J, 33MA)`
    WHEN `the institution's nominee, which is the trustee of an associated trust` THEN `the assets of the associated trust and of the institution, the trustee's own liability being limited to the value of the trust property, including my costs (ss 33K(2), 33M(4), 33MA)`
    WHEN `the institution's nominee, which is not such a trustee` THEN `the nominee's own assets and the assets of the institution, including my costs (ss 33K(3), 33MA)`
    WHEN `the current holder of the office` THEN `the assets of the institution and of its associated trusts, not the office holder's own assets, including my costs (ss 33L, 33MA)`

@export I have a judgment against, or a settlement with, the institution, its nominee or the current office holder for my abuse claim. What can it be paid from (Civil Liability Act 2003 (Qld) ss 33J-33MA)? The institution and an office holder sued in the name of the office may pay from the institution's assets and those of its associated trusts (the office holder is not personally liable); a nominee may pay from the institution's assets and either its own assets or, if it is the trustee of an associated trust, that trust's assets. Costs of the proceeding are included.
GIVEN `defendant` IS A `The defendant I hold a judgment or settlement against` @desc Whom your judgment or settlement is against: the institution; its nominee that is the trustee of an associated trust; its nominee that is not such a trustee; or the current holder of the office
GIVETH A `What my judgment or settlement can be paid from`
`What can my judgment or settlement be paid from` MEANS
    `ss 33J-33MA -- what the liability is paid from` `defendant`
